These are the steps to upgrade an existing store front application (currently opened project) with the "Store Locator" extension by installing the necessary code to the destination application.

# Step 1. First make sure the current project has all the right file structure:
- It has a `components` directory under the project root
- It has the file `index.jsx` under pages/home directory

# Step 2. Clone the pwa-kit repo for the specific branch into the tmp folder
- Run `mkdir /tmp/pwa-kit-tmp`
- Run `git clone -b feature/v4-redux/demo1 https://github.com/SalesforceCommerceCloud/pwa-kit /tmp/pwa-kit-tmp`

# Step 3. From the cloned pwa-kit folder, copy `packages/template-chakra-storefront/components/_fake-store-locator` folder into current project's `components` folder.

# Step 4. Apply the following code changes to pages/home/index.jsx. Skip a step if the code change has already been applied.

- Insert the following line at the end of the import block:
`import loadable from '@loadable/component'`

- Insert the following lines at the end of the const declaration block:
`const StoreLocator = loadable(() => import('../components/_fake-store-locator'))`

- Insert the following line in the JSX element return statement, beween the <Seo> and the <Hero> components.
`<StoreLocator />`

# Step 5. Delete the /tmp/pwa-kit-tmp folder and its contents.